---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, legal } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms that apply to use of the Evidence Axis website, and how they relate to the separate terms agreed for a research engagement."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms" meta={[`Last updated ${legal.lastUpdated}`]} />

  <section class="section container">
    <div class="legal measure">
      <p class="legal__intro">
        These terms apply to your use of the {site.name} website. They are separate from the terms
        that govern a research engagement, which are agreed in writing for each project before work
        begins.
      </p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        This website describes {site.name} services and lets you submit an inquiry. Information on it
        is provided for general information about the practice. Prices and service descriptions shown
        here are current at the time of writing and may be updated.
      </p>

      <h2>Inquiries are not a contract</h2>
      <p>
        Submitting the inquiry form starts a conversation. It does not by itself create an engagement
        or an obligation on either side. An engagement begins only when scope, deliverables, timing
        and price are agreed in writing for a specific project.
      </p>

      <h2>How research is conducted</h2>
      <p>
        Research draws on lawful, publicly accessible sources and any information a client chooses to
        share. Findings are based on the sources and boundary defined for the engagement, as of the
        dates checked. Public information changes over time, and a brief reflects the record at the
        time of research.
      </p>

      <h2>What a brief is — and is not</h2>
      <p>
        A brief distinguishes verified fact from reasoned inference and clearly names what cannot be
        established from public evidence. It is decision support, not a guarantee of any business
        outcome. It does not claim access to confidential, private or non-public information, and it
        should not be read as legal, financial or investment advice.
      </p>

      <h2>Project terms govern the work</h2>
      <p>
        Where these website terms and the terms agreed for a specific engagement differ, the
        engagement terms govern that work. This page does not replace tailored contractual terms for
        a project.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The content, design and visual system of this website belong to {site.name}. Deliverables
        prepared for a client are governed by the rights set out in that engagement's terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing details</h2>
      <p>
        The contracting entity, invoicing arrangements and governing-law details for engagements are
        being finalized ahead of launch and are confirmed in each engagement's written terms. This
        page will be updated to reflect them.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__foot mono">
        These are practical, preliminary website terms. They will be reviewed and expanded before
        public launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__intro { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--space-xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
    padding-top: var(--space-s); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .legal p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal__foot { margin-top: var(--space-xl); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-faint); }
</style>
